# ---- Fly pool size (optional — unlimited is the default) ----
# The pool spawns ONE MACHINE PER QUEUED BUILD every tick (the operator, 2026-09-14:
# "we can launch unlimited builders with fly.io"), so the machine count follows
# the queue rather than a number anyone has to maintain.
#   POOL_CAP_MAX   fleet-wide ceiling on live pool machines PER PROJECT.
#                  Unset = unlimited. A per-project number (flags/fly-pool-<p>
#                  or fly/pool-caps.conf) is trimmed by this one. Set it to
#                  spend less money than the queue would; it is the only brake
#                  that reaches every project at once.
#   POOL_AUTOSCALE 0 restores the pre-2026-09-14 behaviour byte-for-byte —
#                  default cap 3, budget = cap - live, projects ticked one after
#                  another, POOL_CAP_MAX ignored. The kill flag, nothing else.
#POOL_CAP_MAX=
#POOL_AUTOSCALE=1

